    para('Assignment 3 proposed 60 open-ended prompts and 180 responses, preceded by an 18-response pilot. The revised freeze expands that design to 160 open-ended prompts plus 40 secondary translation prompts, selected from the later 500-prompt candidate pool. The pilot’s 2360 words and four primary errors are reported in Assignment 3 as initial implementation evidence. The current report analyses the separately archived 600-response final dataset. Its research question, paired prompt design and three primary error categories follow Assignment 3.')
    para('The final evaluation differs materially from the frozen Gemini API procedure. Four responses were evaluated through the API, sixteen through the Gemini web interface, and 580 by Codex using the existing rubric. The API output limit increased from 4096 to 16384 after truncation. The study team reported that human review confirmed the same errors. Candidate confirmations and the 150-response agreement file record that statement as user-reported evidence. Original independent annotations, reviewer identities and review times were not supplied. Instructor approval of these deviations is not documented.')
    heading('Final experimental setup')
    para('The dataset A4_KK200_v1.0 contains 160 open-ended prompts and 40 custom English-to-Kazakh translation prompts with fixed references. The complete prompt set has 50 items at each difficulty level. The open-ended subset contains 40 prompts per difficulty and six task categories with 26 or 27 prompts each. The same Prompt_ID values occur once in each source group. All 600 responses are non-empty. The revised prompt SHA-256 matches the freeze, although the repository filename is selected_200_prompts.csv.')
    para('Assignment 3 requested approximately 120–150 words per response. The final open-ended prompts use difficulty-specific ranges of 80–120 words for Basic, 120–160 for Intermediate, 160–220 for Advanced and 220–300 for Expert. Translation prompts specify source fidelity without a word range. These revised length instructions are assessed using the same frozen word-count rule for all source groups.')
    para('The planned conditions were Gemini 3.6 Flash as the efficient baseline, GPT-6 Astra as the strong baseline, and Claude Sonnet 5.5 as the main comparison condition. The workbook records the source labels GPT, Gemini and Claude without verifiable snapshot identifiers. Consequently, tables retain those source labels. Prompts and responses are archived verbatim. Collection controls such as fresh chats and disabled tools were intended, but the workbook cannot verify their execution for every response. Source dates are missing for 541 responses.')
